@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy on one server
+
+The root `config/deploy.yml` deploys the open-source Fizzy app in one container:
+SQLite for the database, Solid Queue jobs (including recurring jobs) supervised by
+Puma, Solid Cache, Solid Cable, and local file storage. Kamal Proxy runs alongside
+it and obtains and renews Let's Encrypt certificates. You don't need MySQL,
+Redis, S3, or a separate job server. The `saas/` deployment is for 37signals and
+is not needed here.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed, reachable over SSH as root using your
+  SSH key. If you use another user, add `ssh: { user: your-user }` to the config;
+  that user must have permission to run Docker.
+- A hostname whose DNS A record (and AAAA record, if present) points to this
+  server. Allow inbound TCP ports 80 and 443 for HTTPS and certificate issuance,
+  and SSH from your deployment machine. Don't put another web server on 80/443.
+- An SMTP service that can deliver mail from your chosen sender address. Login
+  codes are sent by email, so working outbound mail is required.
+- On your deployment machine: Git, the Ruby version in `.ruby-version`, Bundler,
+  and Docker with Buildx running. Fork and clone the repo, then `bundle install`.
+  Use the open-source bundle (`SAAS` unset or `false`, no `tmp/saas.txt`).
+
+## Configure
+
+1. Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+   - Set `servers.web` to your server's IP address or SSH hostname.
+   - Set `proxy.host` and `env.clear.APP_FQDN` to your public hostname, without
+     `https://` or a path.
+   - Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` and the `SMTP_*` settings for your mail provider.
+     The example uses authenticated SMTP with STARTTLS on port 587. For port
+     465, set `SMTP_TLS: "true"` and `SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"`.
+     For a trusted unauthenticated relay, remove `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION` and set
+     the username/password secrets to empty values. Only disable STARTTLS if
+     your relay explicitly requires it and the network is trusted.
+   - Set `builder.arch` to match the server (`amd64` or `arm64`). Adjust
+     `WEB_CONCURRENCY` and `JOB_CONCURRENCY` to fit its resources if needed.
+
+   The default local registry needs no account: Kamal runs it on the deployment
+   machine and uses an SSH tunnel to make the image available to the server.
+   Keep Docker running locally during deployment. You can instead configure an
+   external registry using [Kamal's registry options](https://kamal-deploy.org/docs/configuration/docker-registry/).
+
+2. Copy the secrets example and restrict access:
+
+   ```sh
+   cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+   chmod 600 .kamal/secrets
+   bundle exec rails secret
+   ```
+
+   Paste the generated value into `SECRET_KEY_BASE` and enter your SMTP
+   credentials. Generate browser push keys with:
+
+   ```sh
+   bundle exec ruby -rweb-push -e 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+   ```
+
+   Copy both values into `.kamal/secrets`. Keep the secret key and VAPID pair
+   stable across deploys; changing them invalidates sessions or push
+   subscriptions. This setup uses `SECRET_KEY_BASE` directly, so you don't need
+   a Rails master key. `.kamal/secrets` is ignored by Git, and `.kamal/` is
+   excluded from Docker builds. Never put secret values in `env.clear` or commit
+   them. Keep a secure backup of the secrets.
+
+3. Commit your configuration and application changes. Kamal builds from the
+   committed Git tree by default; uncommitted application changes aren't included.
+
+## Deploy
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+This builds and deploys the image, starts the proxy, and prepares all SQLite
+databases through the Docker entrypoint. Visit `https://your-hostname`, create
+an account, and confirm you receive a login email. `bundle exec kamal setup`
+(or `kamal setup` with the bundled Kamal on your PATH) uses the same root config.
+
+For subsequent releases, commit changes and run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+Useful commands:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal logs
+bin/kamal console
+bin/kamal shell
+```
+
+## Persistent data and backups
+
+The named Docker volume `fizzy_storage` is mounted at `/rails/storage`. It holds
+all four production SQLite databases (primary, queue, cache, cable), uploaded
+files, and local data exports. Both old and new app containers use it during a
+deploy. Keep the volume name and mount unchanged; don't delete it or prune Docker
+volumes when cleaning up images.
+
+Persistence is not a backup: losing the server or deleting the volume loses the
+data. Back up the entire volume off-server regularly, along with your secrets.
+For a simple consistent filesystem backup, stop the app with `bin/kamal app stop`,
+snapshot/copy the volume, then `bin/kamal app start`. This stops jobs as well as
+web writes and causes downtime. Don't copy live SQLite database files without
+SQLite-aware backup tooling (including WAL handling). Test restoring the data
+and file ownership for the container's UID/GID 1000 before relying on backups.
+
+## Checking configuration changes
+
+Run `bundle exec ruby test/deployment-test` to validate the single-server layout,
+Kamal secret mappings, and production mail/storage settings without a server.
+This does not replace a real deployment test of DNS, TLS, and SMTP delivery.
diff --git a/test/deployment-test b/test/deployment-test
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..abef120
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/deployment-test
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env ruby
+# Run with: bundle exec ruby test/deployment-test
+# Boots production in subprocesses without contacting Docker, SMTP, or a database.
+require "bundler/setup"
+require "minitest/autorun"
+require "erb"
+require "json"
+require "kamal"
+require "open3"
+require "yaml"
+
+class DeploymentTest < Minitest::Test
+  ROOT = File.expand_path("..", __dir__)
+  DEPLOY = YAML.safe_load(ERB.new(File.read(File.join(ROOT, "config/deploy.yml"))).result, aliases: true)
+  PROBE = <<~'CODE'
+    require "json"
+    puts JSON.generate(
+      smtp: ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings,
+      mail_urls: ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options,
+      route_urls: Rails.application.routes.default_url_options,
+      force_ssl: Rails.application.config.force_ssl,
+      assume_ssl: Rails.application.config.assume_ssl,
+      storage: Rails.application.config.active_storage.service,
+      queue: Rails.application.config.active_job.queue_adapter,
+      databases: ActiveRecord::Base.configurations.configs_for(env_name: "production").to_h { |c| [c.name, c.database] }
+    )
+  CODE
+
+  def test_single_server_layout
+    assert_equal [ "web" ], DEPLOY.fetch("servers").keys
+    assert_equal 1, DEPLOY.dig("servers", "web").size
+    assert_equal true, DEPLOY.dig("proxy", "ssl")
+    assert_equal 80, DEPLOY.dig("proxy", "app_port")
+    assert_equal [ "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage" ], DEPLOY.fetch("volumes")
+    assert_equal DEPLOY.dig("proxy", "host"), DEPLOY.dig("env", "clear", "APP_FQDN")
+    assert_equal "sqlite", DEPLOY.dig("env", "clear", "DATABASE_ADAPTER")
+    assert_equal "true", DEPLOY.dig("env", "clear", "SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA")
+    refute DEPLOY.key?("accessories")
+    assert_includes DEPLOY.dig("env", "secret"), "SECRET_KEY_BASE"
+    refute DEPLOY.dig("env", "clear").key?("SMTP_PASSWORD")
+  end
+
+  def test_kamal_configuration_and_secrets
+    raw = Kamal::Configuration.load_raw_config(config_file: Pathname.new(File.join(ROOT, "config/deploy.yml")))
+    raw[:secrets_path] = File.join(ROOT, ".kamal/secrets.example")
+    config = Kamal::Configuration.new(raw, version: "deployment-test")
+    assert_equal [ "web" ], config.roles.map(&:name)
+    DEPLOY.dig("env", "secret").each do |key|
+      refute_empty config.env.to_h.fetch(key), "Missing example secret: #{key}"
+    end
+  end
+
+  def test_production_settings_from_template
+    config = production_config("SMTP_USERNAME" => "mailer", "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "test-password")
+    assert_equal "smtp.example.com", config.dig("smtp", "address")
+    assert_equal 587, config.dig("smtp", "port")
+    assert_equal "mailer", config.dig("smtp", "user_name")
+    assert_equal "test-password", config.dig("smtp", "password")
+    assert_equal "plain", config.dig("smtp", "authentication")
+    assert_equal true, config.dig("smtp", "enable_starttls_auto")
+    assert_equal false, config.dig("smtp", "tls")
+    assert_equal({ "host" => "fizzy.example.com", "protocol" => "https" }, config.fetch("mail_urls"))
+    assert_equal config.fetch("mail_urls"), config.fetch("route_urls")
+    assert_equal true, config.fetch("force_ssl")
+    assert_equal true, config.fetch("assume_ssl")
+    assert_equal "local", config.fetch("storage")
+    assert_equal "solid_queue", config.fetch("queue")
+    assert_equal %w[ cable cache primary queue ], config.fetch("databases").keys.sort
+    assert config.fetch("databases").values.all? { |path| path.start_with?("storage/") }
+  end
+
+  def test_implicit_tls
+    config = production_config("SMTP_PORT" => "465", "SMTP_TLS" => "true", "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "false")
+    assert_equal 465, config.dig("smtp", "port")
+    assert_equal true, config.dig("smtp", "tls")
+    assert_equal false, config.dig("smtp", "enable_starttls_auto")
+  end
+
+  def test_unauthenticated_relay_and_custom_hostname
+    config = production_config("SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => nil, "SMTP_USERNAME" => "", "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "",
+      "SMTP_DOMAIN" => nil, "APP_FQDN" => "boards.example.org")
+    assert_nil config.dig("smtp", "authentication")
+    assert_nil config.dig("smtp", "user_name")
+    assert_nil config.dig("smtp", "password")
+    assert_equal "boards.example.org", config.dig("smtp", "domain")
+    assert_equal "boards.example.org", config.dig("mail_urls", "host")
+    assert_equal "boards.example.org", config.dig("route_urls", "host")
+  end
+
+  def test_settings_remain_optional_outside_kamal
+    config = production_config("APP_FQDN" => nil, "SMTP_ADDRESS" => nil)
+    assert_equal "localhost", config.dig("smtp", "address")
+    refute config.fetch("route_urls").key?("host")
+  end
+
+  private
+    def production_config(overrides = {})
+      env = DEPLOY.dig("env", "clear").transform_values(&:to_s)
+      env.merge!(DEPLOY.dig("env", "secret").to_h { |key| [ key, nil ] })
+      env.merge!("RAILS_ENV" => "production", "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => "deployment-test-only-#{'a' * 64}",
+        "DISABLE_SSL" => nil, "FORCE_SSL" => nil, "ASSUME_SSL" => nil)
+      stdout, stderr, status = Open3.capture3(env.merge(overrides), "bin/rails", "runner", PROBE, chdir: ROOT)
+      assert status.success?, "Production boot failed:\n#{stdout}\n#{stderr}"
+      JSON.parse(stdout.lines.last)
+    end
+end
